# Prettier is owned at the repo ROOT, not by frontend/ — it resolves its config
# by walking UP from each file, so a config living in frontend/ was invisible to
# e2e/ and everything else, and an ad-hoc `npx prettier` there silently applied
# prettier's defaults (double quotes, 2-space, 80 cols). Keep this file and
# prettier.config.js together at the root: the ignore file is resolved from the
# CWD, so splitting them makes behaviour depend on where the command was run.

# --- Package managers ---------------------------------------------------------
package-lock.json
pnpm-lock.yaml
yarn.lock
bun.lock
bun.lockb
node_modules/

# --- Build output / generated -------------------------------------------------
/frontend/build/
/frontend/build-demo/
/frontend/.svelte-kit/
/frontend/.svelte-kit-dev/
/frontend/.svelte-kit-tiles/
/frontend/static/
/frontend/src/lib/paraglide/
/backend/pb_public/
/backend/pb_public_demo/
/dist/

# --- inlang-managed (only project.inlang/settings.json is ours to touch) ------
/frontend/project.inlang/.meta.json
/frontend/project.inlang/README.md
/frontend/project.inlang/cache/

# --- Machine-owned: Go writes these, so Go's formatting wins ------------------
# backend/cmd/appendseed rewrites items.json with json.MarshalIndent("  ", "  ").
# Prettier would collapse the arrays and re-indent with tabs, so every operator
# append would land a ~5,800-line reformat and a red format:check.
/backend/seed/*.json
# CI's per-pipeline Go module cache ([D-60]): thousands of machine-owned files.
# Also gitignored, which Prettier 3 honours; listed so the ignore is explicit.
/.gomod/
# The opencode agent's own session tooling writes this at runtime; it is
# machine exhaust, not repo style.
/.opencode/

# --- YAML: hand-aligned, and it stays that way --------------------------------
# Prettier does not drop YAML comments, but it does collapse the padding that
# aligns trailing ones (`pnpm check   # …` → `pnpm check # …`). The YAML files
# here (.woodpecker/, compose, goreleaser, tools/dex) are hand-maintained and
# deliberately aligned.
*.yml
*.yaml

# --- Markdown: prettier's table alignment is worse than what we write ---------
# It pads every table cell to the widest cell in its column. docs/internals/design.md has Notes
# cells over 800 characters, so each row becomes a ~1,000-column line and a
# one-word edit re-pads the whole table. There is no option to turn that off,
# and the prose conventions here (hard-wrapped AGENTS.md, unwrapped spec docs)
# are deliberate.
*.md

# Coverage reports (CI's frontend-test, [D-203]): generated, and ignored by
# frontend/.gitignore, which prettier does not read.
frontend/coverage/
